<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Experiments</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Experimental Setting</h3>

<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Models.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate our method on a diverse set of 10 open-source LLMs from three major families: Llama, Gemma, and Qwen. The Llama family includes <em id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Llama-2-7b-chat-hf</em>, <em id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Llama-2-13b-chat-hf</em> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">16</a>]</cite>, <em id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Meta-Llama-3-8B-Instruct</em>, and <em id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct</em> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>]</cite>, while the Gemma series features <em id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">gemma-2b-it</em> and <em id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">gemma-7b-it</em> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>]</cite>. From the Qwen family, we assess <em id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Qwen-1.8B-Chat</em>, <em id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.8" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Qwen-7B-Chat</em> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite>, <em id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.9" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct</em>, and <em id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.10" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct</em> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite>. These models vary in size and architecture, covering instruction-tuned aligned variants.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Metrics.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Activations.</span> We additionally examine the <em id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">refusal direction</em>’s <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>]</cite> change when padding is introduced. To this end, we calculate the similarity between the normal refusal direction created using the normal harmless and harmful prompts (<math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>), and the ones with <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> prepended pad tokens (<math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math>). Formally:</p>
<table id="A1.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{(k)}=\frac{1}{L}\sum_{l=1}^{L}\cos\bigl(r^{l},r_{(k)}^{l}\bigr)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>L</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{(k)}=\frac{1}{L}\sum_{l=1}^{L}\cos\bigl(r^{l},r_{(k)}^{l}\bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Generation quality.</span> <em id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.2.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">BARTScore</em> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>]</cite>, which estimates generation quality from model likelihood without requiring gold references.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Experimental Results</h3>

<figure id="A1.F5" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.01238v1/r_score_vs_padding_size.svg" id="A1.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:286/172;" width="286" height="172"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 5: </span>Refusal direction similarity V.S. padding size.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Activations.</span> In <a href="#A1.F5" title="In A.2 Experimental Results ‣ Appendix A Experiments ‣ Silent Tokens, Loud Effects: Padding in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, we present the refusal direction’s similarity across padding sizes. We notice very similar results to the activation similarity metric. This does make sense, since the refusal direction is created using activations of prompts.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.F6" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.01238v1/bart_score_vs_padding_size.svg" id="A1.F6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:286/172;" width="286" height="172"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 6: </span>BARTScore V.S. padding size.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Generation quality.</span> In <a href="#A1.F6" title="In A.2 Experimental Results ‣ Appendix A Experiments ‣ Silent Tokens, Loud Effects: Padding in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, we present the BARTScore <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>]</cite> of generations across padding sizes. Results act very similarly to the BERTScore measure.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.F7" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.01238v1/bias_scores_pair_full.png" id="A1.F7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/291;" width="476" height="291" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 7: </span>Full bias results on all demographic categories, on L3.1-8B.</figcaption>
</figure>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Bias.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In <a href="#A1.F7" title="In A.2 Experimental Results ‣ Appendix A Experiments ‣ Silent Tokens, Loud Effects: Padding in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>, we present the full impact of the padding size on all the demographic categories in BBQ.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Example Generations</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To illustrate model behavior under different evaluation settings, we provide sampled prompt–response pairs from each analysis axis that includes generation (generation, bias, and safety). For each axis, examples are shown across the range of padding sizes considered.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Generation Analysis</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prompt:</span> Are you a human?</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.T1" class="ltx_table">
<p id="A2.T1.2" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="A2.T1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_align_center ltx_inline-block" style="font-size:70%;width:345.0pt;">
<span id="A2.T1.2.1.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<span class="ltx_tbody">
<span id="A2.T1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_tr" style="--ltx-bg-color:#99FFFF;">
<span id="A2.T1.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="A2.T1.2.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:34.1pt;--ltx-bg-color:#99FFFF;">
<span id="A2.T1.2.1.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.T1.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Padding Size</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A2.T1.2.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left">
<span id="A2.T1.2.1.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="--ltx-bg-color:#99FFFF;">
<span id="A2.T1.2.1.1.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.T1.2.1.1.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Response</span></span>
</span></span></span>
<span id="A2.T1.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_tr" style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;">
<span id="A2.T1.2.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="A2.T1.2.1.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:34.1pt;--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;">
